1-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 09-12-2015, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T07:26:53-07:00","id":661868,"title":"","content":"Hyped as hell for this. Wondering if Dual Kith will be updated in the 2e core book - it ended up being a HUGE part of how I customized my 1e characters. Refluffed dual-kith Coyote/Succubus as nine-tailed fox, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T09:10:49-07:00","id":662000,"title":"","content":"If one can dual kith one will end up with fighter characters that are exceptionally brutal or Blightbent/Oni characters who can make a place uninhabital (poison smog plus extreme weather conditions).<br /> <br /> I was a bit disappointed that Romantic/Succubus wasn\u2018t included, but the kiths seem really cool.<br /> <br /> One question, if a Guargauan gets the 4 dot heavy weapon fighting style merit, does that include the lower 1-3 dots of that merit, or is it only the fourth dot.<br /> <br /> Looking at these Kiths I'd say I'd be Darkling Gremlin in real life, stuff seems to break what I touch it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-12-2015, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T09:20:20-07:00","id":662005,"title":"","content":"Moonborn are hard to gage when you don't know what the Lunacy Condition looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T12:05:17-07:00","id":662084,"title":"","content":"I will travel across the land,<br /> Searching far and wide.<br /> Each Changeling to understand<br /> The power that's inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T13:22:21-07:00","id":662127,"title":"","content":"So wait, are Wizened now more akin to constructs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T13:27:04-07:00","id":662128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=662127#post662127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, are Wizened now more akin to constructs?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-wizened/\" target=\"_blank\">The seeming writeup's been out for over two months.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T14:02:45-07:00","id":662182,"title":"","content":"I had a cool idea for a Darkling Hunterheart.<br /> <br /> Horror Movie monsters. Cenobites like Pinhead, Killers wearing someone elses skin, the Aliens from the alien movies.<br /> <br /> My personal favourite would be a Cenobite.<br /> <br /> Instead of pins, it would have large predator fangs sprouting from its head. Corpse grey skin and the eyes of a tiger, always crying tears of dark blood. Its voice always seems to suggest forbidden desires, no matter what is actually said.<br /> <br /> Its touch would cause wounds to sprout on a targets body from invisible torture impliments (brawling damage is lethal).<br /> <br /> Its gaze could fill someone with enough terror to run screaming or fill them with so many agonizing pleasures as to leave them insensite ( gaze causes the frightened or insensate condition).<br /> <br /> It has a innate sense of human ananomy, it knows where to hurt you so it can easily hit you were you most vulnerible spots. (No penalty to called shots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T14:31:03-07:00","id":662211,"title":"","content":"I like that. Sounds quite eerie.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if the Author, Chatelaine, and Minstrel might have a slight snag in their mechanics. All three gain an automatic success on certain types of rolls, which means that a Wizened member of one of these Kiths who embraces writing, protocol, or music as their unique talent never has to worry about their Seeming Curse (unless, of course, the Wizened's Curse has changed between drafts). Granted, this is a pretty niche issue, but it might still pose a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T15:44:38-07:00","id":662310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=662211#post662211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that. Sounds quite eerie.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if the Author, Chatelaine, and Minstrel might have a slight snag in their mechanics. All three gain an automatic success on certain types of rolls, which means that a Wizened member of one of these Kiths who embraces writing, protocol, or music as their unique talent never has to worry about their Seeming Curse (unless, of course, the Wizened's Curse has changed between drafts). Granted, this is a pretty niche issue, but it might still pose a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Agreed. I prefer to keep Wizened in the &quot;valuable, even respected... but to creepy to intimate&quot; zone..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T16:29:59-07:00","id":662376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=662127#post662127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, are Wizened now more akin to constructs?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Kind of like magical cyborgs. They replaced obsolete body parts with tools of their trade in order to perform better. Great... now I realized Inspector Gadget is probably a Wizened Slewfoot!<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Also, I'm reading several merits that don't seem to be in the core rule book I possess. Such as Telepathy and the Thief of Fate. Is there a 2nd edition core book I'm not aware of? I've heard God Machine has some updated rules, but I don't like the setting enough to buy the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-12-2015, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T16:34:44-07:00","id":662379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=662376#post662376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like magical cyborgs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems as good an opportunity as any to point out that the Seeming affinities for Contracts appear to be intact and to remind everybody what the first Wizened affinity Contracts were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I'm reading several merits that don't seem to be in the core rule book I possess. Such as Telepathy and the Thief of Fate. Is there a 2nd edition core book I'm not aware of? I've heard God Machine has some updated rules, but I don't like the setting enough to buy the book. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">The rules update portion is free</a> and the entirety of the published 2e bluebook material, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T16:46:08-07:00","id":662410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=662379#post662379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">The rules update portion is free</a> and the entirety of the published 2e bluebook material, man.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't know that. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T18:24:46-07:00","id":662497,"title":"","content":"Continueing my Darkling Hunterheart idea, I've decided Ivory Court with mantle of 5 dots.<br /> <br /> This act of joining the Ivory Court changed Ceno, our Darkling Hunterheart, first had words written in liquid gold burned onto his black tongue, words written in ancient greek, those who have read them say they dark prayers to depraved gods that even the true fae fear.<br /> <br /> Then as Ceno went up in the ranks of the Ivory Court, torture implements made from ivory, gold, emeralds, and bull leather appeared on Ceno's person. Ceno never uses them, but when Ceno causes lethal damage with his touch, or torments someone with his gaze, his torture impliments, which stay hanging from his belt unused, become blood spattered for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-12-2015, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T18:32:00-07:00","id":662498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=662000#post662000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one can dual kith one will end up with fighter characters that are exceptionally brutal or Blightbent/Oni characters who can make a place uninhabital (poison smog plus extreme weather conditions).<br /> <br /> I was a bit disappointed that Romantic/Succubus wasn\u2018t included, but the kiths seem really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was why it cost 2-3 merit dots in 1e. They ain't getting it for free.<br /> While I'm also a little on-edge, they are only 75% done. We've literally got a quarter of the kiths left, and as far as I know the plan was to transfer over every kith save for those with redundancy. (Don't need Waterborn, Swimmerskin, AND Waterdweller in 2e, when they're basically the same kith as Elemental, Beast, and Ogre.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T19:00:05-07:00","id":662511,"title":"","content":"Ceno gained a three dot retainer, thanks to his high mantle, his dark priestess, Amber, a former nun who had lost her faith in the Christian God, only to find her faith again in a new God, Ceno. <br /> <br /> Amber had been a Cheerleader at a Christian University, when she'd decided that jesus was calling her to serve, so she joined a nunnery.<br /> <br /> With a year her faith was waning, as a nun she'd seen to much suffering, which her weathy upbringing had hidden her from (wealth that she no longer had access to, her parents did not approve of her becoming a nun).<br /> <br /> She missed her wealth and priveledge.<br /> <br /> It was at this moment of anguish and despair that Ceno appeared to her in dreams, he showed her dark miracles, and she became greedy for them.<br /> <br /> Amber soon after became his Priestess, his sacred whore, serving him faithfully in his enlighten depravity.<br /> <br /> He taught her to enjoy her suffering. Amber now has money, faith, and answers all that she desired, but that just fans the flames of her greed.<br /> <br /> She's greedy for dark miracles, clients (she sees them as parts of her collection hoarding them from competitors), and expensive things. <br /> <br /> Ceno rewards her service (including a tilith of her income) with depraved dreams, trips to the hedge, and his gaze, which Amber has developed a taste for. <br /> <br /> Amber is a gorgeous red head and very charming and most people have no idea she has a dark side to herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-12-2015, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:44:37-07:00","id":663165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=662211#post662211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that. Sounds quite eerie.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if the Author, Chatelaine, and Minstrel might have a slight snag in their mechanics. All three gain an automatic success on certain types of rolls, which means that a Wizened member of one of these Kiths who embraces writing, protocol, or music as their unique talent never has to worry about their Seeming Curse (unless, of course, the Wizened's Curse has changed between drafts). Granted, this is a pretty niche issue, but it might still pose a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Dave's given it some thought. Here was his logic when BrilliantRain asked about asked about extreme dice pools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574731#post574731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. If people want to crank their Skills to avoid their drawback, that's fine. Their &quot;drawback&quot; really means &quot;more Beats&quot;. So all they're doing is missing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, I don't think any Kiths had the &quot;can never fail on a(n) ____ roll&quot; benefits last time. That does feel like a different case to me, that gap between, &quot;has a remote chance&quot; and, &quot;literally has no chance.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in hearing any thoughts Dave has on that. Odds are good it's crossed his mind. It's also possible Wizened write-up may have changed slightly to account for that. We haven't seen exactly what's happening with the Wizened's mechanical downside (nor those for most Seemings), much as he mused about a possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574720#post574720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Benefits:<br /> <br /> 1) Coping mechanism/Clarity gain thing.<br /> <br /> 2) A mechanical boost to your escape thing.<br /> <br /> Drawbacks:<br /> <br /> 1) A thing that risks Clarity, adds to your list of risks.<br /> <br /> 2) A thing that makes your Changeling experience a little more complicated mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/574570-second-edition-wizened?p=574731#post574731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe once [Wizened] start an extended action, they can't stop it without spending Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T09:12:16-07:00","id":663206,"title":"","content":"After looking at the Kiths again, I'm getting a nagging feeling the Lurker makes a better larcenist than the Larcenist. Isolated, their Blessings work well for the way they're described, but when compared to each other... I dunno, I think they're bit off.<br /> <br /> But maybe I'm talking out of my ass. The only concrete detail that makes me scratch my head is how the permanent benefit for the Lurker seems focused on swipey fingers only rather than their wider role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-13-2015, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T13:02:24-07:00","id":663413,"title":"","content":"The new kiths look so frikkin' cool. Can't believe there are even more to come out! (75% done you say?)<br /> <br /> Some minor nitpicks tho'<br /> <br /> The bloodbrute concept is really cool, but two of the blessings sort of... work against each other? You get a bonus to unarmed attacks and improvised weapons, but I always figured that you'd use an improvised weapon to avoid using an unarmed attack... and if you are good at unarmed attacks, you'd rather do them (with lethal damage) than using an improvised weapon. Most improvised weapons would do bashing damage after all, I'm guessing?<br /> Not sure if it needs change or replacement but it just feels a bit redundant. Maybe 1/1 armor instead of the improvised weapons to show how they learned to shake off blows in the fighting pits or something.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the author seems significantly weaker than most other kiths. The ability to read any language is pretty frikkin' cool (like really cool!), but getting one success on expression rolls concerning writing is not so cool. I'm aware is not about the perfect balance or anything, but still... Maybe turn writing with expression into a rote action or give them 8-again or something a bit more powerful.<br /> <br /> Imagine being an Artist kith trying to write that poem, getting +3 (if spending glamor) and only needing 3 success for a critical success. Not to mention the artist can do it with EVERYTHING, not just writing. It can be making (and performing) a song, smithing a two-handed sword and building your own car. All with the same kith. Comparing the two really makes Author seem like the shorter end of the stick. Again, I know it is not about making it the perfect balanced game, but the difference in strength is pretty big right there!<br /> <br /> As a side-note, I frikkin' love the trolls, being from Sweden I picture trolls more like cunning tricksters rather than the dumb brutes of DnD. &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T13:07:07-07:00","id":663415,"title":"","content":"Weapons do lethal. Always. So a bloodbrute will do +0 lethal unarmed and +[durability-1] lethal with anything they happen to grab when a fight starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T13:09:10-07:00","id":663416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663415#post663415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weapons do lethal. Always. So a bloodbrute will do +0 lethal unarmed and +[durability-1] lethal with anything they happen to grab when a fight starts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my mistake then! Then all is good with the improvised weapon thing. I assumed hitting someone with a bottle or a frying pan was bashing!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Additional question. The mirror-skins change, how big can it be? I'm assuming you can't change height and gender, but could you change skin-color? Hair-color? Eye-color? Hair-length? Are the limitations what a skilled crew of make-up artists can do or is it <u><i><b>magic?</b></i></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T14:07:20-07:00","id":663472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663413#post663413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new kiths look so frikkin' cool. Can't believe there are even more to come out! (75% done you say?)<br /> Imagine being an Artist kith trying to write that poem, getting +3 (if spending glamor) and only needing 3 success for a critical success. Not to mention the artist can do it with EVERYTHING, not just writing. It can be making (and performing) a song,<b> smithing a two-handed sword and building your own car</b>. All with the same kith. Comparing the two really makes Author seem like the shorter end of the stick. Again, I know it is not about making it the perfect balanced game, but the difference in strength is pretty big right there!</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with the bolded section of your comment, those are tools not works of art. Though you could make works of art that resemble those tools, but they'd be non-functional.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T14:34:34-07:00","id":663489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663413#post663413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, the author seems significantly weaker than most other kiths. The ability to read any language is pretty frikkin' cool (like really cool!), but getting one success on expression rolls concerning writing is not so cool. I'm aware is not about the perfect balance or anything, but still... Maybe turn writing with expression into a rote action or give them 8-again or something a bit more powerful.<br /> <br /> Imagine being an Artist kith trying to write that poem, getting +3 (if spending glamor) and only needing 3 success for a critical success. Not to mention the artist can do it with EVERYTHING, not just writing. It can be making (and performing) a song, smithing a two-handed sword and building your own car. All with the same kith. Comparing the two really makes Author seem like the shorter end of the stick. Again, I know it is not about making it the perfect balanced game, but the difference in strength is pretty big right there!</div> </div> </div> </div>One possible counter-argument concerns negative modifiers. Even after stacking on the Glamour-fueled blessing, high Attribute and Ability ratings, and whatever else, it's still possible for the Artist to find circumstances that are just too much. The Author, though, is guaranteed at least one success, full-stop, no matter how absurd the penalties and difficulty might become (provided things aren't flatly impossible), as well as a separate flavorful bonus. Though this logic holds up less well in the face of the Minstrel, who gets an automatic success to <i>all</i> Expression rolls, in addition to a different flavorful bonus.<br /> <br /> It's difficult to set the Author and Minstrel's separate bonus side-by-side. Through the Hedge, it's possible to easily* and quickly reach distant places, where reading the local language would be more valuable than it looks &quot;on paper.&quot; Likewise, we don't have the rules for harvesting Glamour: we can expect it's good, but we don't know how good an exceptional success on the roll actually is.<br /> <br /> All that said, I admit my gut feeling is also that Authors could maybe use a little more than they have.<br /> <br /> * For an unknown and likely variable value of &quot;easily.&quot; &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 2e Kiths Preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Artist</b><br /> <u>Blessing:</u> When making a Crafts or Expression roll to create a new work of art (which can be anything from a cake to a symphony), the artist only requires 3 successes (instead of 5) to achieve an Exceptional Success. If he spends a point of Glamour, for the next scene he also adds +3 to his rolls to create this work.<br /> <br /> <b>Author</b><br /> <u>Blessing:</u> The author can never fail an Expression roll to tell or write a story. She automatically achieves one success on such rolls, in addition to the roll results. Also, she can read and interpret anything written in a mortal language.<br /> <br /> <b>Minstrel</b><br /> <u>Blessing:</u> The changeling can never fail on an Expression roll. She gains one automatic success on any Expression rolls. When using Expression in an attempt to harvest Glamour, she achieves exceptional success on three successes instead of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, one other note on the Artist, as I couldn't find another place to mention it. It may be noteworthy that the Artist blessing specifies creating a <i>new</i> work of art. That definitely feels more specific than just making any work of art, though there's a bit of wiggle room. Not saying whether that's good or bad, only that the Minstrel and (mostly) the Author lack it. I'mma babble inquiries about it, just in case it was meant to be more exacting or helps me settle on something.<br /> <br /> The description says creating a cake counts, which is fair, but does the cake count as a new work of art if it's being made while trying to follow a recipe? In a similar vein, while writing a part in a play or improvising a role would certainly fit, would acting out a part in a script or telling a story -- even one the Artist wrote? Like most actors or storytellers, the Artist would no doubt try to put a personal spin on each performance/cake (even if under direction), but is that enough to count as a new performance? Is it enough to count every time the Artist performs it? Even if specifically asked to replicate the way it was done before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T17:36:05-07:00","id":663604,"title":"","content":"The biggest disappointment for me is the Larcenist, which seems half-done (or two-thirds, really). Looking at the others - I want to give it Sleight of Hand, maybe with a bonus/tweak. It brings the power level up to par and you'd want/need it to do the things the Larcenist is described as doing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should add I had this thought after like an hour of straight squee and gleeful brainstorming. This is a big, quality meal of a preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:44:22-07:00","id":663685,"title":"","content":"The Authors ability to pretty much write and tell new stories and read any mortal language would make them worth they're weight in gold in Toronto, in fact they might be broken in that city.<br /> <br /> Other cities they might be under powered.<br /> <br /> One cool thing is that Authors could write to each other in a dead mortal language that no one else understands, in order to keep mesages secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-13-2015, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T18:49:29-07:00","id":663697,"title":"","content":"I Think Lurker is the burgerlar/pick pocket archtype, and Larcenist is more con artist, distract/bullshit you while I steal your shit archetype, so while Larcenist has some extra ability at stealing, its an meant to be used in they're in a more social con job scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-13-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T20:00:35-07:00","id":663783,"title":"","content":"I think we're looking at 25-30 more kiths on top of this. <br /> <br /> I believe they will be:<br /> <br /> Steepscrambler<br /> Windwing (Moonglider Windwing Darkling?)<br /> Romancer (Succubus is Romancer Darkling)<br /> Cleareyes<br /> Pishacha<br /> Ask-Wee-Da-Eed<br /> Apsara (might be eaten by Romancer)<br /> Di-Cang<br /> Shadowsoul<br /> Flamesiren (fire as hypnotic instead of scary or smart)<br /> Wiess Frau<br /> Treasured<br /> Daitya (might fall under Render)<br /> Fatemaker (this one depends on they're plans for Talecrafting)<br /> Inventor (might get eaten by Maker and Smith)<br /> Soldier (Fairest Prince Charming/knight in shining armour, Orger giant warrior, Wizen one with her weapons)<br /> Paradindo<br /> Miner<br /> Drudge (Cinderella would make a cool Fairest Drudge, think about it)<br /> <br /> We know Romancer ate Succubus, and Swimmerskin ate Waterborn, and I'm betting Windwing will eat Moonglider, Gandharva will be eaten by Ministrial.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong about my guesses, maybe Romancer ate Apsara and now its blessing is a mix striking looks without the drawback and vice manipulation, but still that leaves room for new ones, I'm thinking 4 to 10 new kiths?<br /> <br /> Slewfoot is already a new kith and really cool (one of my favourites of the kiths).<br /> <br /> So we have at least some idea of what we have to look forward to and some surprises.<br /> <br /> Possible kith ideas<br /> <br /> Royals (someone else suggested it, I don't remember who)<br /> Wizards<br /> Religious figures (could fall under Di-Cang)<br /> Pied Piper<br /> Medusa/Cockrice turn you into stone kith?<br /> Just some guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-13-2015, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:07:05-07:00","id":663817,"title":"","content":"Dave made another Kith for our playtest session. I dunno if it's going to be in the Core book, but I look forward to spoiling it. (Soon!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:33:29-07:00","id":663831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663817#post663817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dave made another Kith for our playtest session. I dunno if it's going to be in the Core book, but I look forward to spoiling it. (Soon!)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to spoil it. I'm sick right now, and am scraping by on mobile. <br /> <br /> So, spoil away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:57:06-07:00","id":663877,"title":"","content":"Small point of confusion for the Gargantuan blessing: does the character get <i>four dots in</i> the Fighting Style or the maneuver from <i>the fourth dot of</i> the Fighting Style?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T22:15:13-07:00","id":663893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663831#post663831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're welcome to spoil it. I'm sick right now, and am scraping by on mobile.<br /> <br /> So, spoil away.</div> </div> </div> </div>You heard the man!<br /> SPOIL SPOIL SPOIL!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Small point of confusion for the Gargantuan blessing: does the character get <i>four dots in</i> the Fighting Style or the maneuver from <i>the fourth dot of</i> the Fighting Style? </div> </div> </div>I'd guess it's the fourth dot, coz' there is another kith which gives you the first and second dot in a fighting style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T22:16:38-07:00","id":663894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663877#post663877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small point of confusion for the Gargantuan blessing: does the character get <i>four dots in</i> the Fighting Style or the maneuver from <i>the fourth dot of</i> the Fighting Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be cleaned up for sure, but based on how they wrote the Venombite blessing I think it means the fourth dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T06:09:26-07:00","id":664181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663783#post663783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible kith ideas<br /> <br /> Royals (someone else suggested it, I don't remember who)<br /> Wizards<br /> Religious figures (could fall under Di-Cang)<br /> Pied Piper<br /> Medusa/Cockrice turn you into stone kith?<br /> Just some guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wizards are kind of covered with Witchtooth. They gain a bonus to occult rolls and have the power to curse others.<br /> <br /> Royals bring some interesting ideas to mind. A Royal Beast would be like something out of Princess Mononoke. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Medusa / Cockatrice would be kind of over powered if they had flat out petrifying abilities. Although their diminished power could be translated into some form of paralyzing gaze.<br /> <br /> Pied Piper would make a good parade master, getting others to follow to march in step with them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T06:30:07-07:00","id":664222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663831#post663831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're welcome to spoil it. I'm sick right now, and am scraping by on mobile.<br /> <br /> So, spoil away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have the game threads up next week in anticpation of the playtests, It'll show up then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-14-2015, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T14:41:35-07:00","id":664826,"title":"","content":"We just played a chapter with the new Kith rules, and they were very well received. I am a little weary on the Coyote and Flowering blessings, as they focus on social maneuver, which don't come up often in the game I'm running. It would be nice to see an additional bonus for brief social actions similar to Demon's <i>Don't I Know You</i> Embed.<br /> I noticed that the Oracle blessing changed since the last preview. I love that the Oracle can ask multiple questions, but the player doesn\u2019t know how many questions will be answered truthfully.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T18:45:05-07:00","id":665158,"title":"","content":"Oh, so question: How does the first part of the Slewfoot's blessing work? Specifically, the first dot in Professional Training grants a dot in Contacts. So is it assumed that upon exiting the Hedge, the changeling just deduces how to get in contact with a group of people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T20:22:05-07:00","id":666360,"title":"","content":"I'm liking a lot of what I'm seeing with the 2nd Ed changeling. Granted I never read the first. So all if this is nearly new to me. But these descriptions have given me a great idea for a character. So I'm looking forward for this one. I just want it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T21:30:32-07:00","id":666448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=663783#post663783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know Romancer ate Succubus, and Swimmerskin ate Waterborn, and I'm betting Windwing will eat Moonglider, Gandharva will be eaten by Ministrial.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong about my guesses, maybe Romancer ate Apsara and now its blessing is a mix striking looks without the drawback and vice manipulation, but still that leaves room for new ones, I'm thinking 4 to 10 new kiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not an expert at all, buuut combining Succubus and Apsara makes a little more sense to me, given their identity in 1e - the whole 'subtly shifting' Romancer thing is pretty different from both the Succubus and Apsara, who are both Vice and manipulation-themed. I mean, it's not entirely implausible to fold all of them in, but both the Apsara and the Succubus are the tempter/corruptor archetype, while the Romancer is a little more neutral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:19:49-07:00","id":667278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=666448#post666448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not an expert at all, buuut combining Succubus and Apsara makes a little more sense to me, given their identity in 1e - the whole 'subtly shifting' Romancer thing is pretty different from both the Succubus and Apsara, who are both Vice and manipulation-themed. I mean, it's not entirely implausible to fold all of them in, but both the Apsara and the Succubus are the tempter/corruptor archetype, while the Romancer is a little more neutral.</div> </div> </div> </div> They've already said that Romancer and Succubus got combined, the Succubus being the Darkling Romancer, but I thought that Apsara would fit in as well. <br /> <br /> Because all three kiths have at they're heart sex, I mean Illes do too potentially, but its not argueibly at the core as it is with Aspara, Succubi, and Romancer.<br /> <br /> I think Apsara and Succubi would be very interesting as aspects of the same kith, because they're so simular in some ways and so different in others. Both are temptresses, but the Succubus is seen as a fallen angel or descendant of lilith, and Apsara serve the Gods as Courtesans, one is seen as usually in the service of good and the other in the service of evil, but they're functionally the same in the sense of using seduction to manipulate the behavior of mortals, abit from different beings. Aspara are almost Angels sort of, while Succubi are demons.<br /> <br /> The Succubus, Apsara, Romancer combo allows so to explore sex in mythology and the difference and simularies.<br /> <br /> Succubus demon, Apsara Celetial Nymph/Angel, Romancer seductionists of legend like Eros, Venus, and more mortal ones ones like Casa Nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:34:28-07:00","id":667357,"title":"","content":"Along those lines, I feel like Lurker and Larcenist should really be combined. They're at least as similar to each other as Romantic and Succubus, if not moreso. They feel much more like an instance of different keepers using the same kith in different ways than two separate Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T12:38:28-07:00","id":667359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=664181#post664181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wizards are kind of covered with Witchtooth. They gain a bonus to occult rolls and have the power to curse others.<br /> <br /> Royals bring some interesting ideas to mind. A Royal Beast would be like something out of Princess Mononoke. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Medusa / Cockatrice would be kind of over powered if they had flat out petrifying abilities. Although their diminished power could be translated into some form of paralyzing gaze.<br /> <br /> Pied Piper would make a good parade master, getting others to follow to march in step with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pied Piper is covered pretty much perfectly by Thusser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:22:13-07:00","id":668067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=667357#post667357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Along those lines, I feel like Lurker and Larcenist should really be combined. They're at least as similar to each other as Romantic and Succubus, if not moreso. They feel much more like an instance of different keepers using the same kith in different ways than two separate Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really, Larcenist is more of a con artist kith, they have some ability to steal, but they do so by conning people, they're a social kith at heart. Lurker is more stealthy, pick pocket, B&amp;E type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T04:31:20-07:00","id":668069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=667278#post667278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've already said that Romancer and Succubus got combined, the Succubus being the Darkling Romancer, but I thought that Apsara would fit in as well.<br /> <br /> Because all three kiths have at they're heart sex, I mean Illes do too potentially, but its not argueibly at the core as it is with Aspara, Succubi, and Romancer.<br /> <br /> I think Apsara and Succubi would be very interesting as aspects of the same kith, because they're so simular in some ways and so different in others. Both are temptresses, but the Succubus is seen as a fallen angel or descendant of lilith, and Apsara serve the Gods as Courtesans, one is seen as usually in the service of good and the other in the service of evil, but they're functionally the same in the sense of using seduction to manipulate the behavior of mortals, abit from different beings. Aspara are almost Angels sort of, while Succubi are demons.<br /> <br /> The Succubus, Apsara, Romancer combo allows so to explore sex in mythology and the difference and simularies.<br /> <br /> Succubus demon, Apsara Celetial Nymph/Angel, Romancer seductionists of legend like Eros, Venus, and more mortal ones ones like Casa Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hhhuh. Did not know that. Little disappointed, unless they somehow gain both benefits. Still, there's an implicit difference between romance and seduction, in the end-goal. I guess the Romancer's 1e blessing was a little tangential to their actual role in Arcadia, which would lead into &quot;okay let's give them a blessing that actually helps with seduction&quot;. Romancer default kinda felt more like a weird dampened version of Mirrorskin...<br /> <br /> If 2e Romancer has a similar benefit to 1e Romancer, though, then yeah, pretty disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T10:14:01-07:00","id":668403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=668067#post668067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, Larcenist is more of a con artist kith, they have some ability to steal, but they do so by conning people, they're a social kith at heart. Lurker is more stealthy, pick pocket, B&amp;E type.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't really make very good con men. A con man wouldn't need Larceny, since they're not really burglars or pickpockets, as much as they would need Empathy (to pick out good marks), Persuasion (to fast talk), and Socialize (to ingratiate oneself with the mark), in addition to Subterfuge. So, one could make a Larcenist con man, sure, but it's not ideal, and they won't gain much use from the Kith's &quot;always on&quot; Larceny bonus (unless they're really bad con men who have to resort to just outright stealing what they want). One of the more social Kiths would probably work much better for a con man.<br /> <br /> Besides, the write up focuses on them being pickpockets more than anything else. Their quote is about being pickpockets, They're described as being &quot;quick and nimble fingered.&quot; The Fairest example uses their looks to &quot;distract from what her hands are doing.&quot; It even says that assuming they're dishonest because of their penchant for thievery is &quot;often furthest from the truth&quot; - which would be a hard sentence to justify if they were natural con men, since dishonesty is pretty much the defining virtue of con men.<br /> <br /> So, they're primary function seems to be as pickpockets (some of whom use lies to distract or trick their targets). The Lurker gets Sleight of Hand for free, so they are also good pickpockets. Simply add a line or two to the description about how some Keepers give them strange rules to abide by and how some Lurkers use social means to facilitate their thievery, then add Subterfuge to the list of Skills that can be boosted by the Lurkers blessing and you have one Kith that serves both roles perfectly well. Even the example Seeming descriptions all seem like they would work equally well for either Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T12:53:26-07:00","id":668678,"title":"","content":"Think of the Larcenist as a Multiclass Face/Rogue type Character, they're not as good at social manipulation as say an Illes in Darkness, nor are they as good as a Lurker at stealing, but they can doa descent amount of both (actually in some social situations where an Illes can use her looks, the Larcenist is better, such as in sunlight or over the phone, so this is a general rule). <br /> <br /> As for the 2e Romancer kith blessing I doubt that it will resemble the 1e Romancer, nor will it look much like the Succubus' blessing, except perhaps striking looks merit, because vice works so much differently then in 2e. I Think, just a guessing, that the Romancers blessing will look like a cross between the Succubus and the Apsara, striking looks merit with the power to manipulate a targets vice, possible granting a bonus to social interactions with the target when you do.<br /> <br /> The 1e Romancers origional blessing is weak enough they may just toss it on top.<br /> <br /> Of course I could be totally wrong and the Romancer's blessing could work totally different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:22:20-07:00","id":668743,"title":"","content":"The subterfuge-related aspect of their blessing aside, I feel that the write-up makes them out to be pickpockets first and foremost. The mention of persuasion reads like one of many possible options due to the arbitrary rules set by a keeper rather than a universal feature of the kith.<br /> <br /> Side note: They might be better than Illes in certain situations, but Flowering blow them out of the water as con men from a mechanical standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:01:13-07:00","id":668778,"title":"","content":"This talk about combining Kiths has me thinking about the Dual Kith merit. On the one hand, I really hope the merit will appear in 2e because I loved the customizability it brought to characters. On the other hand, I think about some of the combos that would be possible with some of the new, more potent, Kiths, and I worry it might be too overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T14:47:25-07:00","id":668845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=668778#post668778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This talk about combining Kiths has me thinking about the Dual Kith merit. On the one hand, I really hope the merit will appear in 2e because I loved the customizability it brought to characters. On the other hand, I think about some of the combos that would be possible with some of the new, more potent, Kiths, and I worry it might be too overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hunch I've been nursing. Remember the passage before the Kith lists? The one discussing both creating new Kiths and mixing-and-matching traits from different Kiths (provided they make sense)? I feel like that could take the place of the Dual Kith merit. It gets across the same idea of customization, and being under ST scrutiny should help avoid particularly broken combinations. If they go this route, a touch more guidance/discussion (if possible) would be welcome.<br /> <br /> Regardless, we'll see how it works out. Kiths being much more robust than in 1e makes having a second one trickier to price out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T19:16:13-07:00","id":669135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=668845#post668845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a hunch I've been nursing. Remember the passage before the Kith lists? The one discussing both creating new Kiths and mixing-and-matching traits from different Kiths (provided they make sense)? I feel like that could take the place of the Dual Kith merit. It gets across the same idea of customization, and being under ST scrutiny should help avoid particularly broken combinations. If they go this route, a touch more guidance/discussion (if possible) would be welcome.<br /> <br /> Regardless, we'll see how it works out. Kiths being much more robust than in 1e makes having a second one trickier to price out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm going to have a Dual Kith Merit in the playtest material I release. I don't know if it'll make the final product. We'll see how people receive it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T23:29:08-07:00","id":669298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669135#post669135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'm going to have a Dual Kith Merit in the playtest material I release. I don't know if it'll make the final product. We'll see how people receive it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a hunch it seems REALLY powerful, seeing how the new kiths are quite powerful compared to the older ones. Will be interesting to hear the feedback from the playtest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T02:35:53-07:00","id":669362,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping it makes it through. There are some concepts that are only really possible with a dual kith, so... maybe the price should be ramped up to make up for the relative power increase.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, worth noting - the mix-and-match thing was also extant in 1e, but it relied on a lot more Storyteller adjudication to make work. Dual Kith is much easier for a Storyteller to accept just by virtue of, y'know, 'we've worked out what an appropriate cost for this is'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","user":"Taveena","date":". 09-18-2015, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T06:56:01-07:00","id":669622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669298#post669298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a hunch it seems REALLY powerful, seeing how the new kiths are quite powerful compared to the older ones. Will be interesting to hear the feedback from the playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, compare it to other things of the same cost. In 1e there were two versions, one for 3 dots that required Wyrd 2, and one for 2 dots if you picked another of your Seeming's Kiths or 3 if you picked a Kith from a different Seeming, and was Character Creation only. Since Kiths aren't tied to Seemings in 2e, let's assume it costs 3 dots, and has some prerequisite. If it's still character creation only, that's about a third of your starting Merit dots. If it still requires Wyrd 2, that's 8 experiences you could be spending on Fighting Styles, or Professional Training and Resources, or Contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T07:16:47-07:00","id":669639,"title":"","content":"One nit-pick: Skitterskulk's triple defense while dodging gives them a potentially huge pool in GMC, which can be exploited with merits like Armed Defense 3. I would recommend either a flat bonus (+2? +4?) to defense while dodging, or to specifically say this bonus does not apply to any merit that allows you to roll dodge as an attack.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T08:34:27-07:00","id":669729,"title":"","content":"I, on the other hand, would make a skitterskulk with that very merit and play MC Hammer's &quot;Can't Touch This&quot; during all combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T09:03:49-07:00","id":669750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669729#post669729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, on the other hand, would make a skitterskulk with that very merit and play MC Hammer's &quot;Can't Touch This&quot; during all combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now imagine that Skitterskulk has dual kith with Levinquick. (MC Thor's Hammer, if you will.) Now you're pretty much immune to Firearms attacks, too. And there's nothing in the rules as written that prevents you from using Armed Defense 3 when being shot at. &quot;He took a shot at that weird electric spider guy, and then he got hit by lightning and just kind of... exploded.&quot; I mean, <i>I wouldn't allow it</i>, but somebody might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T09:10:44-07:00","id":669753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669622#post669622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, compare it to other things of the same cost. In 1e there were two versions, one for 3 dots that required Wyrd 2, and one for 2 dots if you picked another of your Seeming's Kiths or 3 if you picked a Kith from a different Seeming, and was Character Creation only. Since Kiths aren't tied to Seemings in 2e, let's assume it costs 3 dots, and has some prerequisite. If it's still character creation only, that's about a third of your starting Merit dots. If it still requires Wyrd 2, that's 8 experiences you could be spending on Fighting Styles, or Professional Training and Resources, or Contracts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering that several kiths give access to 3 point merits, sometimes improved versions of them, and almost always in addition to other benefits, I think it would need to be more than 3 dots, even with a prerequisite. Looking at the Kiths, I wouldn't hesitate to burn 4 or 5 merit points on many of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T09:41:55-07:00","id":669771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669753#post669753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that several kiths give access to 3 point merits, sometimes improved versions of them, and almost always in addition to other benefits, I think it would need to be more than 3 dots, even with a prerequisite. Looking at the Kiths, I wouldn't hesitate to burn 4 or 5 merit points on many of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Merits give access to more than their dot values worth of other Merits and advantages. Professional Training and Mystery Cult Initiation are good examples. For 3 dots of PT you get 4 exp worth of value (2 dots of contacts and 2 specialties), plus 9-again on 3 skills. For 3 dots of MCI you get 4 exp worth of value (a specialty or 1-dot Merit, a 1 dot Merit, and a Skill dot or 2-dot Merit). From my observation, the kinds of Merits that give a higher return on their initial exp investment are usually Merits that help develop the character by necessitating background details and/or character ties to justify the purchase. I'd say Dual Kith fits that bill, because if it's still character creation only you'll have to account for how both of those Kiths resulted from your durance, and if it's not, you'll need to build your character's story to explain how they went through another change equivalent to what was done to them by their Keeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T10:26:24-07:00","id":669842,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, I like the idea of combining Coyote with Romancer to get a Kitsune/Huli Jing kith - alone, neither of them really represents the dual trickster/seducer nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T10:30:11-07:00","id":669847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669771#post669771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of Merits give access to more than their dot values worth of other Merits and advantages. Professional Training and Mystery Cult Initiation are good examples. For 3 dots of PT you get 4 exp worth of value (2 dots of contacts and 2 specialties), plus 9-again on 3 skills. For 3 dots of MCI you get 4 exp worth of value (a specialty or 1-dot Merit, a 1 dot Merit, and a Skill dot or 2-dot Merit). From my observation, the kinds of Merits that give a higher return on their initial exp investment are usually Merits that help develop the character by necessitating background details and/or character ties to justify the purchase. I'd say Dual Kith fits that bill, because if it's still character creation only you'll have to account for how both of those Kiths resulted from your durance, and if it's not, you'll need to build your character's story to explain how they went through another change equivalent to what was done to them by their Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see your point, but I still think the potency of the 2e kiths is enough to put the merit in the 4+ price range. Their value is even greater than 3 dots of PT or MCI in many cases. Like I said, I wouldn't balk at 4-5 dots cost for a lot of those kiths.<br /> <br /> And I'd say that MCI and PT build a character's ties to the world around them in a way that Dual Kith doesn't. Those merits don't just indicate a backstory, but a connection to organizations and people in the mortal world. Dual Kith on the other hand, just requires that your Keeper had some specialized purpose in mind that was best served by a hybrid kith (or just thought it would be amusing).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(Further on that note: Slewfoot grants the 3 dot PT for Detective in addition to other, not insubstantial, benefits. That's essentially stacking multiple high return merits if you take it as a Dual Kith.)</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T11:14:19-07:00","id":669913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669639#post669639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One nit-pick: Skitterskulk's triple defense while dodging gives them a potentially huge pool in GMC, which can be exploited with merits like Armed Defense 3. I would recommend either a flat bonus (+2? +4?) to defense while dodging, or to specifically say this bonus does not apply to any merit that allows you to roll dodge as an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Armed Defense 3 requires a WP every turn - and can also be exploited with Celerity def twinking, Down the Prey (werewolf isn't much for def, really, but there's this one thing or a custom fetish), and so forth.<br /> <br /> Really my point is that your problem is with Armed Defense 3, not powers that affect defense or dodging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T11:45:11-07:00","id":669943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669847#post669847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point, but I still think the potency of the 2e kiths is enough to put the merit in the 4+ price range. Their value is even greater than 3 dots of PT or MCI in many cases. Like I said, I wouldn't balk at 4-5 dots cost for a lot of those kiths.<br /> <br /> And I'd say that MCI and PT build a character's ties to the world around them in a way that Dual Kith doesn't. Those merits don't just indicate a backstory, but a connection to organizations and people in the mortal world. Dual Kith on the other hand, just requires that your Keeper had some specialized purpose in mind that was best served by a hybrid kith (or just thought it would be amusing).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(Further on that note: Slewfoot grants the 3 dot PT for Detective in addition to other, not insubstantial, benefits. That's essentially stacking multiple high return merits if you take it as a Dual Kith.)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point as well. I think the problem is, it's value is heavily dependent on the Kith you gain with it. I'd be willing to pay 4 or 5 dots for Slewfoot or Razorhand, but not for Airtouched or Manequin.<br /> <br /> At any rate, we'll have to see how it goes in the playtesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T12:05:23-07:00","id":669964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669943#post669943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see your point as well. I think the problem is, it's value is heavily dependent on the Kith you gain with it. I'd be willing to pay 4 or 5 dots for Slewfoot or Razorhand, but not for Airtouched or Manequin.<br /> <br /> At any rate, we'll have to see how it goes in the playtesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Some Kiths are a bargain at even 5 dots, while some are extremely situational or just don't feel like they're worth the points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:08:23-07:00","id":670057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669964#post669964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. Some Kiths are a bargain at even 5 dots, while some are extremely situational or just don't feel like they're worth the points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that more a problem with Kith balance, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T13:24:31-07:00","id":670081,"title":"","content":"The answer is free dual kiths for all. (or only one each).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T14:18:22-07:00","id":670166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=670057#post670057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that more a problem with Kith balance, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T21:52:03-07:00","id":671671,"title":"","content":"You know, some legends attribute the Oni to being formed out of 100 different animals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dual Kith: Oni + Chimera<br /> <br /> &lt;3<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:11:48-07:00","id":671823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=669842#post669842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As mentioned, I like the idea of combining Coyote with Romancer to get a Kitsune/Huli Jing kith - alone, neither of them really represents the dual trickster/seducer nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, you don't need any mechanical benefits though to make such a character work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or simply design your own kith that mix the two without actually overpowering anything by reducing the separate benefits in power and/or effectiveness.<br /> <br /> The intent of the new rules seem to make kiths more powerful and more important storywise (which I wholeheartedly agree with btw, I doubt that any player in my current group with the exception of the mirrorskin is even aware of the kith of the others) in the new edition. If so, why look for a solution that forces the designers into a more stringent role when designing said powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:10:39-07:00","id":671955,"title":"","content":"After some playtesting with my players, the blessing of the Brewer seems a little awkward. The need to touch the liquid feels strange and conspicuous. I think that the power would be better if it allowed to work by touching the recipient holding the liquid. Also, the bonus to <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">resist poisons/intoxication from the 1rst edition is really missed.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T11:24:13-07:00","id":672243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=671955#post671955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After some playtesting with my players, the blessing of the Brewer seems a little awkward. The need to touch the liquid feels strange and conspicuous. I think that the power would be better if it allowed to work by touching the recipient holding the liquid. Also, the bonus to <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">resist poisons/intoxication from the 1rst edition is really missed.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it does seem like it might work a bit better to need only touch the cup holding the liquid. Some small bonus to poison/intoxication would also better fit the &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">often she was forced to test the potency and efficacy of her brews on herself</span></span>&quot; fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T04:57:53-07:00","id":673067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaemonChrno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=671955#post671955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After some playtesting with my players, the blessing of the Brewer seems a little awkward. The need to touch the liquid feels strange and conspicuous. I think that the power would be better if it allowed to work by touching the recipient holding the liquid. Also, the bonus to <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">resist poisons/intoxication from the 1rst edition is really missed.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, after a little argument with my girlfriend, you should add a line to specify if the Brewer Blessing affects the taste of the liquid he changed or if it is undetectable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:37:51-07:00","id":673314,"title":"","content":"Anyone noticed any other cool dual kith combos yet?<br /> <br /> So far I have Nix/Whisperwisp, use the Nix's vocal persuasian power at a distance thanks to the Whisperwisp power, no cellphone needed, and spy while your hidden underwater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:44:16-07:00","id":673319,"title":"","content":"Nix/Author, use your vocal persausion power to to tell a story and get an automatic success.<br /> <br /> Illes/Larcenist, out of sunlight you are a perfect lier, you get the equivilant of striking looks x4, and by spending a couple of glammer you can add wyrd to subetfuge rolls, and if you can use your looks to help sell the lie, you can get an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:03:48-07:00","id":673423,"title":"","content":"As-is I'd set Dual Kith at about 4 dots, maybe 3. No prerequisite Wyrd. Another approach would be to make it a 1-Dot merit that allows you to combine the benefits of two kiths into one thing in some fashion without stacking them on each other (like take the passive benefit from Kith A and layer it on top of the Glamour expenditure of Kith B). A third approach would be a 2 Dot merit that allowed you two Kiths, but only the benefit of one kith at a time (swapping your blessing costs Glamour).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T15:34:38-07:00","id":673479,"title":"","content":"You Kith is supposed to be what your Durance was in Arcadia, right? What if, by virtue of hitting Wyrd 6, your connection to the Wyrd becomes strong enough that you manifest another one based on what you've been doing since you've escaped?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T10:21:31-07:00","id":674369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=673423#post673423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As-is I'd set Dual Kith at about 4 dots, maybe 3. No prerequisite Wyrd. Another approach would be to make it a 1-Dot merit that allows you to combine the benefits of two kiths into one thing in some fashion without stacking them on each other (like take the passive benefit from Kith A and layer it on top of the Glamour expenditure of Kith B). A third approach would be a 2 Dot merit that allowed you two Kiths, but only the benefit of one kith at a time (swapping your blessing costs Glamour).</div> </div> </div> </div>1 and 3 work. 2 is a little tricky because there's gonna be some edge cases where it's not clear how you'd combine 'em.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T11:03:36-07:00","id":674400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=674369#post674369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1 and 3 work. 2 is a little tricky because there's gonna be some edge cases where it's not clear how you'd combine 'em.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Regarding method 2: some Kiths have only a passive/always on power (Author and Coyote, for instance) while others only have powers that have to be fueled with Glamour (such as Brewer and Leechfinger). Besides, I think those sort of blendings of two Kiths are probably better covered by the ST adjudication described under Modifying Kiths. As far as the third option goes, switching Kiths at will creates weird cases where characters lose attribute or skill dots when activating other powers and isn't much of a hindrance in other cases (I think it would lead to a lot of characters having a &quot;combat mode&quot; Kith) making it far too attractive. I think a 4-dot merit with no prerequisite makes sense, possibly with some sort of minor drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T19:05:58-07:00","id":674791,"title":"","content":"The Venombite's focus on grappling is certainly interesting. Not what I was expecting, but still cool. I'm not quite sure what the Grappling merit has to do with being venomous though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, also, is the Venombite's poison moderate or grave?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:10:38-07:00","id":674866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=674791#post674791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Venombite's focus on grappling is certainly interesting. Not what I was expecting, but still cool. I'm not quite sure what the Grappling merit has to do with being venomous though.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, also, is the Venombite's poison moderate or grave?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to have someone grappled to bite them.<br /> <br /> Edit: It says it deals lethal damage, so I would assume Grave for the purposes of the Poisoned Tilt? Otherwise, just Toxicity = Wyrd. There don't seem to be any official guidelines on when a poison should count as moderate or grave... I hope we get advice on that in WoD2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-22-2015, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T20:25:42-07:00","id":674886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have to have someone grappled to bite them. </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, I get that, and I think the bonus to grappling rolls works for that reason. It's just the granting of the Grappling style merit that I don't quite understand. The first dot makes the character immune to the Drop Prone and Take Cover moves, while the second lets the character render someone prone without having to establish a grapple first. It just doesn't feel quite right for the Venombite. The only suggestion I could give as a replacement is maybe that grappling rolls achieve an exceptional success on three successes instead of five, since on an exceptional success the character can use two grappling moves at once, meaning the Venombite is better at poisoning their victim and then slipping away from harm's reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 09-22-2015, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T21:03:42-07:00","id":674915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=674886#post674886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah, I get that, and I think the bonus to grappling rolls works for that reason. It's just the granting of the Grappling style merit that I don't quite understand. The first dot makes the character immune to the Drop Prone and Take Cover moves, while the second lets the character render someone prone without having to establish a grapple first. It just doesn't feel quite right for the Venombite. The only suggestion I could give as a replacement is maybe that grappling rolls achieve an exceptional success on three successes instead of five, since on an exceptional success the character can use two grappling moves at once, meaning the Venombite is better at poisoning their victim and then slipping away from harm's reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah, that's a good point. I'd forgotten what the first two maneuvers in that Style did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T00:48:52-07:00","id":680741,"title":"","content":"I'm a little surprised that no-one has brought it up from a balancing point of view... But what happens if the player takes Jewel-eyes and Riddleseeker/Roteater/Snowskin/Tunnelgrub.<br /> You get +2 to your Attributes and they may exceed the natural limit of 5. Heck, if you take Jewel-eyes and Roteater, does that mean you can start the game with 7 in Stamina?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, it sounds pretty damn cool, but I'm not sure if there is any exp-cost that can make it balanced nor any reason as to why a player who is the slightest bit of gamey would jump the chance to gain that quite powerful buff to their character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T07:29:19-07:00","id":680971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=680741#post680741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little surprised that no-one has brought it up from a balancing point of view... But what happens if the player takes Jewel-eyes and Riddleseeker/Roteater/Snowskin/Tunnelgrub.<br /> You get +2 to your Attributes and they may exceed the natural limit of 5. Heck, if you take Jewel-eyes and Roteater, does that mean you can start the game with 7 in Stamina?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, it sounds pretty damn cool, but I'm not sure if there is any exp-cost that can make it balanced nor any reason as to why a player who is the slightest bit of gamey would jump the chance to gain that quite powerful buff to their character.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Perhaps the Dual Kith merit could have a caveat that duplicate bonuses don't stack. So you could get a plus one to a skill from one Kith and 9 again to the same skill from another, but not plus two to a single skill by combining two Kiths that each have a plus one, for instance.<br /> <br /> I definitely think that looking at the Kiths with Dual Kith in mind makes some imbalance among the Kiths apparent. It would be difficult to correct, though, since many of the Kith benefits are difficult to price. I'm also not sure how concerned the writers are with balancing the Kiths, for that matter. But the imbalance does make setting a value for the Dual Kith merit difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T13:43:27-07:00","id":681379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=680971#post680971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point. Perhaps the Dual Kith merit could have a caveat that duplicate bonuses don't stack. So you could get a plus one to a skill from one Kith and 9 again to the same skill from another, but not plus two to a single skill by combining two Kiths that each have a plus one, for instance.<br /> <br /> I definitely think that looking at the Kiths with Dual Kith in mind makes some imbalance among the Kiths apparent. It would be difficult to correct, though, since many of the Kith benefits are difficult to price. I'm also not sure how concerned the writers are with balancing the Kiths, for that matter. But the imbalance does make setting a value for the Dual Kith merit difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem isn't whether a single kith is balanced or not, it's more that if you include dual-kiths (and they are this powerful) you are basically telling anyone who enjoys making good/powerful characters that they have to take the dual-kith, because if they don't, they are seriously nerfing themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:21:19-07:00","id":681394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681379#post681379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem isn't whether a single kith is balanced or not, it's more that if you include dual-kiths (and they are this powerful) you are basically telling anyone who enjoys making good/powerful characters that they have to take the dual-kith, because if they don't, they are seriously nerfing themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, which is why I was suggesting the whole &quot;no duplicate bonuses&quot; as a potential limitation and why I've been saying I think it should cost at least 4 points (although the more I think about it the more I lean towards 5).<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a drawback, as well. Maybe a permanent version of whatever the 2e version of an endeavor or forbiddance. A character could suffer a sort of geas appropriate to their Kiths as a consequence of having been remade so extensively.<br /> <br /> I was just bringing up the question of balance as an aside.<br /> <br /> Do you think Dual Kith should be left out all together, A_Newfie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T16:24:55-07:00","id":681523,"title":"","content":"I will mention that Dual Kith is not barred from characters after creation, should someone feel left behind,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:45:19-07:00","id":681595,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I'm in the predicament of being ill-versed in 2e nWoD mechanics, while wondering how old 1e Changeling characters might look once updated. Given one character I've got in mind, how useful or potent do people think the Broadback Blessing looks at present (copied below for reference)? In particular, I recall hearing -- perhaps incorrectly -- that opening a PC's Doors isn't really advised; if I'm not wildly off and that advice is followed, how much does that weaken the Blessing?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 2e 75% Kiths Teaser, Broadback</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blessing:</b> The changeling suffers no penalties due to fatigue and injury. The character also adds his Wyrd to his Doors in Social Maneuvering. Spend a point of Glamour as a reflexive action during a social interaction to add his Wyrd to a contested action to a Resistance trait.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681523#post681523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will mention that Dual Kith is not barred from characters after creation, should someone feel left behind</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know. This is using the playtest version Dave's trying to feel out (which may be teased), but which isn't guaranteed to appear in the final release, right?<br /> <br /> Also, I hadn't looked at your signature in a while, Arc, but congrats on the freelancer gigs!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T17:51:08-07:00","id":681599,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It's still being played around with. That said, Dual Kith is such a popular merit, I feel like the odds are good.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks! It got updated today when I sent in my first draft for Beast, but I've actually been on for The Hedge for a while now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T20:35:22-07:00","id":681720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681599#post681599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. It's still being played around with. That said, Dual Kith is such a popular merit, I feel like the odds are good.<br /> <br /> Also, thanks! It got updated today when I sent in my first draft for Beast, but I've actually been on for The Hedge for a while now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Congratulations, indeed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T01:54:31-07:00","id":681855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681599#post681599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. It's still being played around with. That said, Dual Kith is such a popular merit, I feel like the odds are good.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cynic in me tend to assume that if something is popular in a playtest it is a sign of it being too powerful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I honestly feel such a merit is superfluous and asking for balance issues. Just design your own kith that does fit your image or simply refluff an existing one with powers that do match your character concept mechanically, but not story-wise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:43:37-07:00","id":682214,"title":"","content":"I think that it should be left out entierely, yes.<br /> Right now, even if you can get it later, it's still a very clear sign to anyone who remotly cares about how powerful their characters it to get it or suck it, basically.<br /> <br /> The fact that you can get it later or not doesn't really remove the issue. Getting it will be important if you want to be powerful. It's not a flair thing, like recources or contacts or even a fighting style, things that you will get depending on your concept but aren't exactly necessary for you to feel powerful.<br /> <br /> For now, it feels a bit like generation in the first vampire. If you didn't spend points on it, you essentially nerfed yourself.<br /> <br /> The need for dual kiths in the first version of changeling existed, a lot of the kiths were weak to downright terrible, but might fit a certain concept. (I'm looking at you, Skitterskulk/Runnerswift/Soldier)<br /> <br /> I mean, it will of course not be the end of the world, but I could name a few players I know already who would definitely not skip the idea of adding +1 to an attribute along with other bonuses just by buying a merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681855#post681855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cynic in me tend to assume that if something is popular in a playtest it is a sign of it being too powerful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I honestly feel such a merit is superfluous and asking for balance issues. Just design your own kith that does fit your image or simply refluff an existing one with powers that do match your character concept mechanically, but not story-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, I often felt that a majority of the characters I saw with dual-kith in old changeling were there to be power-builds. The reasons were thought up AFTER they had been picked as a powerful combination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T11:06:15-07:00","id":682230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681855#post681855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cynic in me tend to assume that if something is popular in a playtest it is a sign of it being too powerful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I honestly feel such a merit is superfluous and asking for balance issues. Just design your own kith that does fit your image or simply refluff an existing one with powers that do match your character concept mechanically, but not story-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>We should clarify.<br /> <br /> Not one of my players so far has picked up Dual Kith. Granted, some players are still working on theirs, but of the six people I have, no one's going for it so far. When I say Dual Kith is popular, I'm not talking about in the playtest. It's in the playtest docs, certainly, but it's not in Los Angeles or Paris with a character yet.<br /> <br /> So, what did I mean?<br /> <br /> *looks around* Some of our largest threads have been wrapped around the games of coming up with stories based on Dual Kith. Regardless of playtest, the fanbase <i>loves</i> mixing and matching.Of course it's going to be popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T11:10:30-07:00","id":682233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681379#post681379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem isn't whether a single kith is balanced or not, it's more that if you include dual-kiths (and they are this powerful) you are basically telling anyone who enjoys making good/powerful characters that they have to take the dual-kith, because if they don't, they are seriously nerfing themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div> That depends on the value of other merits, without that, its impossible to gage how powerful the dual kith merit is compared to 4 or 5 dot Changeling Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T11:11:36-07:00","id":682234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=681855#post681855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cynic in me tend to assume that if something is popular in a playtest it is a sign of it being too powerful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Arc meant popular among the fan base in general, not popular in the playtests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T11:22:45-07:00","id":682238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=682230#post682230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should clarify.<br /> <br /> Not one of my players so far has picked up Dual Kith. Granted, some players are still working on theirs, but of the six people I have, no one's going for it so far. When I say Dual Kith is popular, I'm not talking about in the playtest. It's in the playtest docs, certainly, but it's not in Los Angeles or Paris with a character yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, One of us in Paris has. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I wasn't sure if I should bring it up, since I tend to err on the side of caution when it comes to NDAs, but my character has it. I don't think she's overpowered by any definition of the word, but we'll see how it goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T12:08:47-07:00","id":682265,"title":"","content":"Remember, if you aren't sure about something, feel free to ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T12:48:56-07:00","id":682282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=682214#post682214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it should be left out entierely, yes.<br /> Right now, even if you can get it later, it's still a very clear sign to anyone who remotly cares about how powerful their characters it to get it or suck it, basically.<br /> <br /> The fact that you can get it later or not doesn't really remove the issue. Getting it will be important if you want to be powerful. It's not a flair thing, like recources or contacts or even a fighting style, things that you will get depending on your concept but aren't exactly necessary for you to feel powerful.<br /> <br /> For now, it feels a bit like generation in the first vampire. If you didn't spend points on it, you essentially nerfed yourself.<br /> <br /> The need for dual kiths in the first version of changeling existed, a lot of the kiths were weak to downright terrible, but might fit a certain concept. (I'm looking at you, Skitterskulk/Runnerswift/Soldier)<br /> <br /> I mean, it will of course not be the end of the world, but I could name a few players I know already who would definitely not skip the idea of adding +1 to an attribute along with other bonuses just by buying a merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I often felt that a majority of the characters I saw with dual-kith in old changeling were there to be power-builds. The reasons were thought up AFTER they had been picked as a powerful combination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly see your point. Personally, I've never had a player take advantage of the merit in that way, but I've only run a couple of chronicles worth of CtL and the players I've run it for aren't prone to that sort of power gaming. I used it for NPCs in a few instances where I wanted to emulate a monster from folklore or had a specific concept that was best described by a combination of two Kiths. When I've had players take it, it was either because they really wanted a Kith from another Seeming, or because they had a good concept. That said, I've certainly gamed with some folks who <i>would</i> abuse it. And with the much more powerful Kiths in 2e, I totally understand why you'd be worried about any player who's slightly concerned with optimizing taking the merit. Still, I'd like a method of combining Kiths that doesn't rely heavily on ST adjudication/sanctioned home-brew. I'm crossing my fingers that the writers can come up with a way of making the merit balanced, but if they can't, I'd rather have the merit available and just be strict about granting ST approval for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T14:43:28-07:00","id":682358,"title":"","content":"Might be my relative unfamiliarity with the system, but power-gaming in NWoD has always seemed kinda weird to me. Like that aforementioned 7-stamina character is ostensibly designed to excel in physical scenes, but because of that overspecialization they can't, really.<br /> Maybe I'm biased just because so many of my concepts were inherently tied TO that dual kith. I've never taken it as a power thing - they are a romancer and an animalistic trickster, so Coyote/Romancer. They are a dragon made of fire, so they are a Draconic/Fireheart. They are a chivalric knight, equally devoted to their lady and their duty, so they're a Romancer/Soldier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T16:43:55-07:00","id":682437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=682358#post682358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be my relative unfamiliarity with the system, but power-gaming in NWoD has always seemed kinda weird to me. Like that aforementioned 7-stamina character is ostensibly designed to excel in physical scenes, but because of that overspecialization they can't, really.<br /> Maybe I'm biased just because so many of my concepts were inherently tied TO that dual kith. I've never taken it as a power thing - they are a romancer and an animalistic trickster, so Coyote/Romancer. They are a dragon made of fire, so they are a Draconic/Fireheart. They are a chivalric knight, equally devoted to their lady and their duty, so they're a Romancer/Soldier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maxing to 7 Stamina out of the gate would probably be a bad idea, but starting at 5 or 6 Stamina would leave you with average or better in your other physicals (assuming physical primary). That's a very appealing build for stat-conscious players. And, although attribute dots are certainly nice, I don't think that's even close to the nastiest combo. The potential for power-gaming is certainly there. Heck, depending on what Romancer does, that Coyote/Romancer might end up being pretty sick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T19:15:30-07:00","id":682585,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling that the 2e contracts and in-core Goblin Vow mechanics might help take some of the fluff slack of dual Kith. Arc would know better than me (no mechanical spoilers necessary) if thats true, but I can imagine, say, your fire dragon would be Draconic, but have contracts with fire, goblin vows with deadly blazes, perhaps join a sun or fire related court. Your romantic soldier could simply be a Fairest Soldier who has both contracts supporting battle as well as poetry and seduction. II'm glad to see Goblin Vows becoming central to the powers of courts, so it seems the rules could also be used for adding other flavors to a changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:21:03-07:00","id":683086,"title":"","content":"I'm not particularly worried about Dual Kith stacking Attributes. Someone has 7 Stamina or 7 Strength or 7 Intelligence... ... So what? It's +2 dice on some rolls and +2 to some derived traits, the game won't explode. It's just not that big of a deal, especially if Dual Kith clocks in at around 3-4 EXP. What you have to worry about is particularly synergistic abilities that are, together, greater than the sum of their parts. I haven't noticed any combinations like that yet but it's a <i>pretty big</i> list.<br /> <br /> Are Goblin Vows going to be in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T07:26:17-07:00","id":683092,"title":"","content":"I feel like you could save a lot of wordcount on these kiths by clarifying how kiths that grant supernatural merits that cost willpower work somewhere earlier in the document, letting you nix explaining that you have to spend Glamour instead of Willpower every single time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T08:03:58-07:00","id":683121,"title":"","content":"<i>Artist </i>-- Cool. Feels like a great fluff choice. I'd like clarification on what you can get out of an exceptional piece of art somewhere in the book. This is also a pretty nice Kith for social maneuvering.<br /> <br /> <i>Author</i> -- I almost want to ask this to be opened up to other skills. Persuasive essays, propoganda posters, etc. should all really fall under this purview.<br /> <br /> <i>Blightbent</i> -- Great all around. Does what I would want it to do if I were playing that type of character.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodbrute</i> -- It feels kind of like a bunch of random mechanical things were thrown into a pot, although that may be the writing style. It's very &quot;she can do this... and this... and this... and this.&quot; Moving the unarmed damage portion closer to the improvised weapon portion and making the transition smoother would help. I'd also love it if the negate surprise component worked on everything, even if you had to make it not-perfect or if you had to make it cost a point of Glamour. The reason is that I feel like Bloodbrutes should *totally* have Ultimate Ninja Warrior contests with deadly result. Like a True Fae pointing at an obstacle course with a thing at the end and saying, &quot;see how far you can get.&quot; That's cool. I'd also like it if Bloodbrutes just got the first dot in the Improvised Weapon Fighting Style instead of sort of getting part of it.<br /> <br /> Off hand something like, &quot;A bloodbrute is always ready for a fight. She gains the first dot in the Improvised Weapon Fighting Style (page XX) for free and her unarmed attacks can inflict 0L damage. By spending a point of Glamour, she can make any roll to detect surprise or a trap (page XX) a Rote action.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Brewer</i> -- Then one day, a Brewer dipped his hand in the pacific ocean and almost all of the world's water into alchohal. This was not as cool as his fraternity said it probably would be--the dead fish smell was just <i>dreadful</i>. <br /> <br /> I'm just being facetious and teasing. ^_^<br /> <br /> A limit on quantity may be prudent, as would a clarification that touching a recepticle that holds the liquid works. Whether or not the brew is obvious to the drinker is also important to determine. Otherwise it's a pretty solid kith.<br /> <br /> <i>Bright One</i> -- Cool power. Does exactly what I'd want it to. How to end the blinded tilt could use better wording. Technically, the blinded tilt implies that the person can't still see the bright one.<br /> <br /> <i>Broadback </i>-- I feel like +Wyrd to doors and +Wyrd to contested rolls is a smidge redundant. Social Maneuvering is rarely used by the ST against player characters. One of those for fluff purposes and for NPCs is great. Together it kind of feels like a wasted choice. I'd also like more &quot;able to drag things for miles without tiring&quot; and less &quot;not gonna listen to you.&quot; I just feel like if I'm taking Broadback, it's for the purposes of doing some impressive thing for a very long time. If you do change one of those, my vote is on keeping +Wyrd to doors and doing something else with the glamour spend portion. +Doors means that other people have to be as tenatious as the Broadback to make headway, which feels appropriate.<br /> <br /> <i>Brollachan</i> -- I keep thinking this is an anime thing for some reason. Probably the -chan at the end of its name. Anyways, it feels like a pretty solid, all around concept. It is by far the most potent combat kith to date. May want to consider nixing the +2 bonus to grapples. The Insensate / Frightened thing is going to be used more by straight up attacking people and less by ambushing them from the shadows and disabling.<br /> <br /> <i>Chatelaine </i>-- Pretty fun kith. I like the immunity and feel like it could lead to a lot of fun. Wouldn't the immunity by default clash with things, though? Getting the free success and the immunity and a glamour spend thing is kind of O_o in the face of the Author only getting the free success and one &quot;other.&quot; It's not a huge deal, though.<br /> <br /> <i>Chimera </i>-- I have some pretty strong concerns about the glamour spend portion of this Kith. Rote action on contested rolls to resist <i>all</i> supernatural powers makes them fairly unassailable by anything that isn't direct physical combat. I mean, ultimately this kith's strength is determined by how frequently contracts and creatures from the hedge rely on those powers, but it sets off my alarms. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T01:17:13-07:00","id":684079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=682358#post682358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be my relative unfamiliarity with the system, but power-gaming in NWoD has always seemed kinda weird to me. Like that aforementioned 7-stamina character is ostensibly designed to excel in physical scenes, but because of that overspecialization they can't, really.<br /> Maybe I'm biased just because so many of my concepts were inherently tied TO that dual kith. I've never taken it as a power thing - they are a romancer and an animalistic trickster, so Coyote/Romancer. They are a dragon made of fire, so they are a Draconic/Fireheart. They are a chivalric knight, equally devoted to their lady and their duty, so they're a Romancer/Soldier.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impact of min-maxing on a game depends heavily on the Storyteller and the group in question, but it does exist and it is not always easy to deal with. Besides, it is not the 7-stamina character that would worry me, but other odd synergies. Mind you, the stats that work on Willpower or other derived stats can have a big impact and avoiding 7s there is probably a good idea...<br /> <br /> Regardless, as I said, the downside of dual kith is powergaming and I just do not see an upside to such a merit. The only reason to pick it is for both game mechanical benefits, since appearances and story are purely fluff and can be easily changed. As others have said, if you want to play a fiery based dragon, just pick the right contracts and skills. It is what I did when I build such a character in 1e, and my storyteller had no issue with making the elemental contract an affinity contract for the character.<br /> <br /> Mind you, in the end when running my game, I can always simply forbid it in my campaign just as I have added Professional Training to the forbidden list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T07:02:42-07:00","id":684387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=684079#post684079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impact of min-maxing on a game depends heavily on the Storyteller and the group in question, but it does exist and it is not always easy to deal with. Besides, it is not the 7-stamina character that would worry me, but other odd synergies. Mind you, the stats that work on Willpower or other derived stats can have a big impact and avoiding 7s there is probably a good idea...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so true. I've seen both ends of the spectrum, from my old LARP group where a 40 defense build was considered fair because it only helped you protect yourself rather than killing other characters, to my current tabletop group where having a dice pool greater than 7 is considered specialized. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=684079#post684079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, as I said, the downside of dual kith is powergaming and I just do not see an upside to such a merit. The only reason to pick it is for both game mechanical benefits, since appearances and story are purely fluff and can be easily changed. As others have said, if you want to play a fiery based dragon, just pick the right contracts and skills. It is what I did when I build such a character in 1e, and my storyteller had no issue with making the elemental contract an affinity contract for the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't agree with this, though. There is a huge story difference between a Draconic who learned some fire-related Contracts after escaping and a Draconic Fireheart. Kiths come from the way your Durance changed you and are therefore an inherent part of your being. Contracts come from deals made with the Wyrd and are therefore inherently external. It's like what your character <i>is</i> vs. what you character <i>does</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=684079#post684079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, in the end when running my game, I can always simply forbid it in my campaign just as I have added Professional Training to the forbidden list.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is always an option, of course, but not the ideal one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T00:43:37-07:00","id":685338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=684387#post684387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't agree with this, though. There is a huge story difference between a Draconic who learned some fire-related Contracts after escaping and a Draconic Fireheart. Kiths come from the way your Durance changed you and are therefore an inherent part of your being. Contracts come from deals made with the Wyrd and are therefore inherently external. It's like what your character <i>is</i> vs. what you character <i>does</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is only because you make it so, especially when you consider that the 1e elemental is not even immune to flames nor can he breath fire either unless he does take said Elemental contract. The power of the 1e fireheart is to spend glamour for extra dice on Wits. The fact that my character's durance was a mix of flames and draconic heritage is nothing but fluff with no mechanical impact (and the fireheart power actually did not fit said character's concept anyway). It was easily changed with no impact on game mechanics, balance or story. It is the power of the kith that that for me ultimately supports the character concept. It is also the only thing other players tend to remember as unique. For example, I could easily see a player select a 1e bright one kith for his flame elemental because that way he can at least give light with his flame (and in fact that power fits the example of Jack from the book a lot better considering his durance as a candle).<br /> <br /> Regardless, the biggest reason I went for dragon kith with that particular PC was because it was part of the fairest. Seeming says a lot more about your character concept than your kith, at least in 1e. In the new edition I would have picked fairest en elemental and just make it look like a dragon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","user":"Madfox11","date":". 10-02-2015, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T07:02:05-07:00","id":685682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=685338#post685338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is only because you make it so,</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's because that's how the book is written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=685338#post685338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially when you consider that the 1e elemental is not even immune to flames nor can he breath fire either unless he does take said Elemental contract. The power of the 1e fireheart is to spend glamour for extra dice on Wits. The fact that my character's durance was a mix of flames and draconic heritage is nothing but fluff with no mechanical impact (and the fireheart power actually did not fit said character's concept anyway). It was easily changed with no impact on game mechanics, balance or story. It is the power of the kith that that for me ultimately supports the character concept. It is also the only thing other players tend to remember as unique. For example, I could easily see a player select a 1e bright one kith for his flame elemental because that way he can at least give light with his flame (and in fact that power fits the example of Jack from the book a lot better considering his durance as a candle).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about 1e. If you want to re-fluff that's your prerogative, but that's not actually a replacement for dual-kith, since as written there is, in fact, a significant story difference between Kiths and Contracts, especially in 2e where the interaction between one's kith and seeming is a hugely defining part of the character both mechanically and in terms of backstory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=685338#post685338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, the biggest reason I went for dragon kith with that particular PC was because it was part of the fairest. Seeming says a lot more about your character concept than your kith, at least in 1e. In the new edition I would have picked fairest en elemental and just make it look like a dragon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But in 2e, which is what we were discussing, Kith and Seeming both say different, equally important things about your character (how their Durance changed them and how they changed themselves in order to escape.) Also, Elemental and Fairest are both Seemings, so you wouldn't be able to be both. At any rate, I was only using the Draconic Firehart to continue your example. The specifics of this character you played one time are really tangential to my argument, which is that Kith means something in the narrative, and Contracts mean something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:04:19-07:00","id":685792,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the Draconic/Fireheart Dual Kith that came up was a friend's character who was a dragon literally made of lava, a la Deathwing. (Might've actually been Stonebones with Contracts of Elements (Magma). Both seem apt.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T02:06:36-07:00","id":689494,"title":"","content":"Lets just agree to disagree, in that I feel that an unique kith is better to deal with a dragon made out of flames is a better idea than using a dual kith if only because I feel that such a thing is neither a dragon nor a burning elemental <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T03:13:31-07:00","id":696904,"title":"","content":"Winkyfaces fill me with a terrible and senseless rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T11:09:08-07:00","id":697576,"title":"","content":"I like you Enokh, but I've got this five-year old in me you shouldn't have told that too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Madfox, sure, you can do that. Charlaquin's right as far as canon goes, but hey, your table, your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-11-2015, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T06:41:01-07:00","id":699659,"title":"","content":"Not everyone will want to build unique kiths, dual kith merit gives them another option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T22:35:22-07:00","id":737014,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=683121#post683121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Author</i> -- I almost want to ask this to be opened up to other skills. Persuasive essays, propoganda posters, etc. should all really fall under this purview.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodbrute</i> -- It feels kind of like a bunch of random mechanical things were thrown into a pot, although that may be the writing style. It's very &quot;she can do this... and this... and this... and this.&quot; Moving the unarmed damage portion closer to the improvised weapon portion and making the transition smoother would help. I'd also love it if the negate surprise component worked on everything, even if you had to make it not-perfect or if you had to make it cost a point of Glamour. The reason is that I feel like Bloodbrutes should *totally* have Ultimate Ninja Warrior contests with deadly result. Like a True Fae pointing at an obstacle course with a thing at the end and saying, &quot;see how far you can get.&quot; That's cool. I'd also like it if Bloodbrutes just got the first dot in the Improvised Weapon Fighting Style instead of sort of getting part of it.<br /> <br /> <i>Chatelaine </i>-- Pretty fun kith. I like the immunity and feel like it could lead to a lot of fun. Wouldn't the immunity by default clash with things, though? Getting the free success and the immunity and a glamour spend thing is kind of O_o in the face of the Author only getting the free success and one &quot;other.&quot; It's not a huge deal, though.<br /> <br /> <i>Chimera </i>-- I have some pretty strong concerns about the glamour spend portion of this Kith. Rote action on contested rolls to resist <i>all</i> supernatural powers makes them fairly unassailable by anything that isn't direct physical combat. I mean, ultimately this kith's strength is determined by how frequently contracts and creatures from the Hedge rely on those powers, but it sets off my alarms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of thought up my own House Rules and optional interpretations on the blessings of those kiths.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u>Author:</u> The Changeling gains the 8-again rule to all Expression, Persuasion, and Subterfuge rolls related to writing and other wordy endeavors. In addition, she gains three dots in the Pledgesmith Merit, and can read and interpret any mortal language.<br /> <br /> <u>Bloodbrute:</u> The Bloodbrute gains the Danger Sense Merit and the three-dot version of the Improvised Weaponry Style, and deals lethal damage with his hands and feet. Any improvised weapons he is armed with do not suffer damage with each strike. Furthermore, any time she would roll Wits + Composure to detect ambushes and traps, she can spend a point of glamour to add automatic successes equal to her Wyrd.<br /> <br /> <u>Chatelaine:</u> The Chatelaine gains the Bureaucratic Navigator Merit, as well as three dots in the Etiquette Merit. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Additionally, she may spend a Glamour to add her Wyrd to Presence and Manipulation rolls for the rest of the scene. </span></span><br /> <br /> <u>Chimera</u>: The Chimera gains a +2 bonus to all social rolls with creatures from the Hedge, and gains 8-again on all contested rolls against Contracts and other supernatural powers. He may also spend glamour to either make a contested roll against a supernatural power rote, or cancel out a power which subtracts a Resistance trait from its roll.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> I have more for the other kiths (as well as ideas for a couple of the 1E kiths that haven't been ported over) if you guys are interested. Basically, the house rules I posted here are for those who might have issue with the automatic success aspects of certain kiths. Going into specfics, I wanted to make the Author's kith blessing more defined and versatile, especially since the flavor text attached to it hints that his words and writing can have a <i>potent</i> effect to them. The Pledgesmith Merit is from 1E.<br /> <br /> The Chatelaine's power was something I wanted to tone down for similar reasons. But I reimagined it so that it could work similarly to the Troll in the sense that it has a Style Merit for Social Maneuvering. The Bureaucratic Navigator Merit is also from 1E.<br /> <br /> My personal twist on the Chimera's blessing was meant to emphasize the fact that they can be very effective in dealings with Hedgebeasts and Hobgoblins, and good tanks against supernatural powers. It's an entirely different story for mundane persons and methods, though.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-29-2015, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T14:08:44-07:00","id":739583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/660537-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths-75?p=683086#post683086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not particularly worried about Dual Kith stacking Attributes. Someone has 7 Stamina or 7 Strength or 7 Intelligence... ... So what? It's +2 dice on some rolls and +2 to some derived traits, the game won't explode. It's just not that big of a deal, especially if Dual Kith clocks in at around 3-4 EXP. What you have to worry about is particularly synergistic abilities that are, together, greater than the sum of their parts. I haven't noticed any combinations like that yet but it's a <i>pretty big</i> list.<br /> <br /> Are Goblin Vows going to be in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, look at the mantle merit in the court creation document, it granymts access to a goblin vow related to your court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T19:49:50-07:00","id":740665,"title":"","content":"With regards to kiths that will appear in Changeling Second Edition, has there been any word of the Cleareyes being included as well? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}